          AcademyLessonSection('3. Operations and quality', '''Operations management designs and improves processes that produce goods and services. Capacity planning, inventory management, procurement, scheduling, logistics and quality assurance influence cost, reliability and customer experience. Lean methods seek to reduce activities that do not add value, while continuous improvement uses repeated measurement and problem solving.

Quality is not simply final inspection. It should be designed into processes through standards, training, supplier controls, process capability and feedback. Evaluate operations using a balanced set of measures such as defect rates, lead time, service reliability, safety and total cost.'''),
